# One sentence per mod: what it is good for in a Vanilla survival game and how far it reaches into Vanilla. Facts from code and manuals only.
V = {
"simplelib": "Shared base of the Simple mods with a modpack guide and warped wart (found in bastion chests); it reorders creative tabs and hooks hoppers, anvils and the Wither, but anvil crushing, the Wither drop, the legendary choir and the Free Look key switch on only when a Simple mod asks.",
"simplebuilding": "Adds tools, blocks and gear on top of a normal survival world, but it also reaches into Vanilla: its pools join the loot of 14 kinds of structure chests and of fishing treasure (switchable per structure, scalable with one factor); its offers join the villagers and the wandering trader (switchable); world generation adds four small End structures, cracked-ice fields and sculk jaws (ice fields switchable), and the bundled Simple Ores adds two End ores (switchable in its own config); new armor stands get arms and swap armor with you, sneaking with small items such as sticks or ingots places them on blocks, XP orbs merge, and repairs without a new enchantment keep the anvil cost (each switchable); hammocks speed up the time of day while enough players rest in them (factor 1 turns it off).",
"simplearrows": "Gives archers a use for the Vanilla Fletching Table (right-click opens an arrow workbench) plus a light arrow and, with Simple Ores, a silver arrow; Vanilla arrows and bows keep working unchanged.",
"simplebeacons": "Gives late-game players stronger beacons and conduits to build towards; the Vanilla conduit stays as it is, and the Vanilla beacon only gains range from Gold, Emerald, Diamond and Netherite pyramid blocks (switchable).",
"simpleblocks": "Fills gaps in Vanilla building blocks (missing stairs, slabs, walls and variants) so builders find the shape they need. Only a few Vanilla behaviors change: falling snow leaves a thin snow cap on fences, walls, stairs and slabs, and pumpkins, melons and hay age in the Pale Garden; both can be switched off, and Frost Grass, which would turn snowy grass into a mod block, is off by default.",
"simplebuildingtools": "Speeds up large builds with wands, colored octants and the Blueprint; it only acts when you hold the tool, and it hooks the cartography table for blueprint copies.",
"simplechallenges": "Offers an optional world mode with free and locked areas for players who want a harder start; without a chosen challenge it changes nothing.",
"simpleslabs": "Adds thin building pieces cut from blocks that already have a slab, for finer detail; it only adds its own blocks and recipes and changes no Vanilla block or recipe.",
"simplechisels": "Lets you step a block along its family (stone, chiseled, cracked, stairs, slabs) in the world instead of crafting it; no Vanilla recipe or block is replaced.",
"simplecrucibles": "Adds a fuel-free cooking station for the mid game, a sturdier cauldron and soul lava, a rare Nether fluid in the world generation (can be switched off); the iron bucket breaks when it pours soul lava, and copper buckets carry water and lava (never soul lava) and also work on the Vanilla cauldron.",
"simpledimensions": "Lets server owners add and tune extra dimensions and portals with checked destinations; the Vanilla dimensions keep their terrain, and Nether portals may also be built as arches (on by default).",
"simpleearth": "Turns a very high flight into a view of the world as a cube; below that height the game is Vanilla, and it hooks the client sky, clouds and weather rendering.",
"simpleenchanting": "Gives players two upgraded enchanting tables for higher tiers (the second needs Simple Ores); the Vanilla enchanting table works as before.",
"simpleenddragonfight": "Makes the Vanilla dragon fight tougher and fairer for groups (a health bar per player, a faster dragon, extra minions); it changes the fight, not the End itself.",
"simpleend": "Adds new wood, plants and two biomes on the outer End islands for players who explore past the dragon; the biomes replace only rare patches of the outer islands and never touch the dragon island, and the bundled Simple End Dragon Fight (switchable) scales the dragon fight with the number of players.",
"simplefoundry": "Lets you melt gold, copper and iron and cast it again in a multiblock, one ingot per ingot; Vanilla smelting is unchanged.",
"simplefun": "Adds small playful items and toys, each capped by the server. On by default and each switchable: throwing items far while sneaking, throwing bricks with right click, a pig head after eating pork (milk undoes it) and Knockback IV; breaking glass with bricks is off by default.",
"simplegadgets": "Gives builders and miners hand-held helpers (gauge, transposer, detector, attractor, rod); they work while held (the Detector and Attractor also when placed), and a few client mixins add HUD and view effects.",
"simplehammers": "Adds sledgehammers that mine 3x3, reshape and upgrade blocks; they are tools and enchantments on top of Vanilla, with hooks on mining speed, anvil and a few recipes.",
"simplelayers": "Adds a sky dimension above y 700 and a Backrooms dimension below the bedrock for explorers; the Overworld below and above stays Vanilla, with small piston and block-state hooks for the new blocks.",
"simplelights": "Adds thin lamps that can sit on any block side so builders can light rooms neatly; Vanilla lamps are unchanged.",
"simplemachines": "Gives redstone players stronger pistons, faster hoppers, a double piston, a signal dampener, a Smither and an Auto Crafter that needs no redstone clock (the Vanilla Crafter makes one item per pulse); Vanilla pistons, hoppers and the Crafter stay as they are. The Reinforced Piston moves one unbreakable block only when paid with a Redstone Block, the breaker pistons wear out and ask claim mods first; the upgrades extend the piston logic by mixin.",
"simplemaps": "Gives explorers endless maps per dimension with waypoints and picture maps; Vanilla maps keep working. The map screen and locator bar get client hooks; the web export is off by default.",
"simplemobheads": "Gives every mob a collectible head for decoration and note blocks, dropped when a charged creeper kills the mob; no Vanilla loot table is replaced.",
"simplemoney": "Adds a currency, weighted villager trades and treasure loot so survival worlds get an economy. Making a bill is deliberately expensive (two diamonds plus gold, iron and resin each), so money is a sink for diamonds and gold, not a loophole. Villagers and the wandering trader get extra offers (a few Vanilla goods for bills, goods of other Simple mods for bills, bills for diamonds); Vanilla offers stay in the pool and no Vanilla loot table is replaced. Offers that remove Vanilla scarcity (budding amethyst, diamond ore) are off by default.",
"simplemusic": "Lets players write sheet music, press discs and carry a pocket jukebox; Vanilla discs and the jukebox still work, with hooks to play uploaded discs.",
"simpleoctets": "Adds eighth-size blocks cut from their full block so builders get finer detail; the Vanilla blocks stay as they are. Two changes to Vanilla inputs - sneak-placing a melon slice and corner breaking with a sledgehammer - can each be switched off in the server config.",
"simpleovens": "Gives smelting-heavy players faster furnace, smoker and blast furnace tiers and furnace minecarts, upgraded in the world; the Vanilla furnaces are not replaced.",
"simplepads": "Adds launch, flight, potion and teleport pads plus stronger pressure plates for travel and automation; Vanilla elytra and wind charges work as before, with small hooks for the spawn elytra.",
"simplequestionary": "Explains any item you put in a table, for newcomers; it adds no gameplay of its own and does not change any Vanilla behavior.",
"simplerespawn": "When another player is near, replaces instant death with a downed state a teammate can revive; this is a clear change to how death works in multiplayer.",
"simpleriding": "Improves mounts (faster saddles, higher jumps, nautilus dashes, mount armor and horseshoes) so riding is worth it; the Vanilla mounts stay and are only tuned. The server checks how fast a mount may move, so fast saddles cannot be abused to teleport.",
"simpleshops": "Lets players sell goods from a block and a display case on a server; Vanilla villager trading is untouched.",
"simplesandwiches": "Adds sandwiches built on a cutting board, with butter and cheese from a milk cauldron; Vanilla food is not changed.",
"simplestorage": "Gives players more storage (crates, tiered chests and shulker boxes, bundles, quivers, backpacks); the Vanilla containers stay, and some mixins touch chest, shulker, bundle and arrow pickup behavior.",
"simpletrims": "Adds four armor trim templates (glowing, emitting, pulsating, inverting), placeable templates and trim upgrades for players who like armor looks; Vanilla trims are unchanged. Armor with the Radiance upgrade and held torches, lanterns and lava buckets place invisible light blocks in the world (only the mod's main switch turns this light off).",
"simpletweaks": "Keeps older worlds loading and adds server claims that are on by default; the claim rules change who may build where on a server. Also on by default: partial keep inventory (hotbar and armor stay on death), a death hint, AFK players not counting for sleeping, newcomer protection and a dragon egg after every dragon fight; each can be switched off.",
"simplechess": "Gives builders decoration and real board games on their builds; it only adds its own blocks, items and recipes and changes no Vanilla behavior.",
"simplevault": "Gives explorers a rare find in the bedrock with riddles and a reward; the Vanilla bedrock stays except at the rare gap, and a few hooks handle its pistons and block states.",
"simplewanderers": "Gives every village a wandering trader with a horse and, in return, moves the everyday half of the Vanilla Wandering Trader's goods (47 of his 78 common goods) to him; the traveling trader keeps the rest, plus anything other mods add to the Vanilla trade lists. Off in the config, the Vanilla trader is untouched.",
}

